The memory pool table entry of GlobalToStorage.TryGenerateRawStorageOp from a two-level index the host writes after the
entries (a word per 2 MiB chunk below 2^40, 512-word page tables for the chunks several entries share) instead of the
chunk hint and the binary search. The driver inlines the lookup function at every global memory access: the 13 unrolled
search steps made OoT's foliage mesh shaders (some 500 accesses) 1-2 MB of machine code at 255 registers,
and an access to a pool smaller than a chunk took 13 dependent loads.

